SCOPE: clean. The attempt-2 manifest lists 4 files
(handlers_sweep.go, handlers_sweep_test.go, conversion-sweep.html,
web/static/css/tailwind.css); the working tree additionally carries
handlers.go, whatif.html and render_conversion_sweep_test.go, all of which are
attempt-1 changes still uncommitted on the same branch and all authorized by
the brief. .swarm/ledger.tsv is lead bookkeeping. No critical glob touched.
tmp/tailwind.check.css is a build artefact of my own `make css-verify` and is
gitignored. `git status --porcelain` is byte-identical before and after my
verification run apart from the other lane's verdict file appearing -- I
created and edited nothing in the repo; both probes ran through
`go test -overlay` from the scratchpad.
Live instance: :8080 was never contacted, killed, restarted or rebuilt over.
`make build` writes ./budget2, which replaces the file on disk but cannot
disturb the already-running process (it holds the old inode); this was
required by the brief.

BOTTOM LINE: 7 of 7 criteria met with cited evidence. Both attempt-1 defects
are fixed and independently reproduced: the deflation matches
tax_optimizer.go:236-241 field-for-field, the fixture makes real and nominal
diverge by ~10.5% on the asserted row, and a mutation test proves the new
test -- and only that test -- fails when the nominal path is restored.
